{
  "sn24.3:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.3 ",
  "sn24.3:0.2": "1. Stream-Entry ",
  "sn24.3:0.3": "This is My Self ",
  "sn24.3:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.3:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.3:1.3": "‘The self and the cosmos are one and the same. After death I will be that, permanent, everlasting, eternal, and imperishable’?” ",
  "sn24.3:1.4": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn24.3:2.1": "“When form exists, because of grasping form and insisting on form, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.3:2.2": "‘The self and the cosmos are one and the same. After death I will be that, permanent, everlasting, eternal, and imperishable.’ ",
  "sn24.3:2.3": "When feeling … ",
  "sn24.3:2.4": "perception … ",
  "sn24.3:2.5": "choices … ",
  "sn24.3:2.6": "consciousness exists, because of grasping consciousness and insisting on consciousness, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.3:2.7": "‘The self and the cosmos are one and the same. After death I will be that, permanent, everlasting, eternal, and imperishable.’ ",
  "sn24.3:3.1": "What do you think, mendicants? ",
  "sn24.3:3.2": "Is form permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn24.3:3.3": "“Impermanent, sir.” … ",
  "sn24.3:3.4": "",
  "sn24.3:3.5": "",
  "sn24.3:3.6": "",
  "sn24.3:3.7": "",
  "sn24.3:3.8": "“Is feeling … ",
  "sn24.3:3.9": "perception … ",
  "sn24.3:3.10": "choices … ",
  "sn24.3:3.11": "consciousness permanent or impermanent?�